{"duration_api_ms":51095,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"b6c36b1d-1bb0-4f04-9615-6915bca2a9fe","total_cost_usd":0.1651514,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25122,"cache_read_input_tokens":40427,"output_tokens":5657,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1624},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25122,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2040,"cache_read_input_tokens":30887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3775},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5657,"cacheReadInputTokens":40427,"cacheCreationInputTokens":25122,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1651514,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1624,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"Enable a persistent host firewall on node1 (firewalld active, enabled, and permanent config in place)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"firewalld was already active/enabled at baseline; executor added persistent (--permanent) rules for ssh and 8080/tcp, set zone target to REJECT, and reloaded. /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml on disk shows the persisted config, and post-reboot the same config was confirmed intact with firewalld active/enabled.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d107a6a41b744c99\",\"cmd-a6b52ea9171c46ac\",\"cmd-953425bdcd824c85\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Permit SSH inbound\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"firewall-cmd --list-all shows ssh service allowed both at runtime and permanent; nftables filter_IN_public_allow chain accepts tcp dport 22; sshd confirmed listening and healthy pre- and post-restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d107a6a41b744c99\",\"cmd-7ef75988122f4e4d\",\"cmd-953425bdcd824c85\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Permit TCP port 8080 inbound\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"firewall-cmd shows 8080/tcp added and persisted; nftables allow chain accepts tcp dport 8080; live curl test to the node's external IP on 8080 returned HTTP 200 confirming functional reachability through the zone rules.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d107a6a41b744c99\",\"cmd-7ef75988122f4e4d\",\"cmd-c36bc3202faa49f4\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Reject unrelated inbound connections\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Zone target set to %%REJECT%%; nftables filter_IN_public chain falls through to 'reject with icmpx admin-prohibited' for traffic not matching the allow chain (only 22/8080). Pre-existing unrelated allowances (cockpit, dhcpv6-client) were removed so only ssh+8080 remain. The self-curl test on port 9999 returned content rather than a clean rejection, but this is explained and consistent with loopback (iifname lo accept) bypassing the public-zone chain rather than a real misconfiguration — the nftables ruleset directly shows the reject fallback applies to the eth0-bound public zone.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b39b793c55464edc\",\"cmd-deed77eb98f64c31\",\"cmd-c36bc3202faa49f4\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id (4a743885...) and firewalld health captured; systemctl reboot issued and acknowledged; subsequent poll timed out confirming disconnect; post-restart boot_id (2a24f144...) differs, confirmed by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots as well; firewalld, persisted zone config, nftables rules, and sshd were all re-verified healthy after the restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7e44e795edde44b5\",\"cmd-09c8fa3c79e1459e\",\"cmd-2934e7b357fa4d93\",\"cmd-7c1d8292f3044eac\",\"cmd-953425bdcd824c85\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"State-changing commands were limited to the firewalld reconfiguration (required), removal of unrelated pre-existing service allowances (required to satisfy the 'reject unrelated' outcome), temporary test HTTP listeners on 8080/9999 used for bounded functional verification, and the restart itself. The test listeners were killed and confirmed absent from the socket table (cmd-f766d31253d84359, cmd-a6b52ea9171c46ac), but their log/pid files (/tmp/http8080.log, /tmp/http8080.pid, /tmp/http9999.log, /tmp/http9999.pid) remained in the after-executor temporary-files snapshot as minor uncleaned residue — low-risk and non-functional but not fully reverted.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b39b793c55464edc\",\"cmd-c36bc3202faa49f4\",\"cmd-f766d31253d84359\",\"cmd-a6b52ea9171c46ac\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task — a persistent firewalld configuration on node1 permitting only SSH and 8080/tcp while rejecting other inbound traffic — are directly supported by firewall-cmd, nftables, and live-port evidence, and the configuration was confirmed to survive an actual node restart (differing boot_id, recovered firewalld/nftables/sshd state). The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also completed with clear pre/post boot-identity and health evidence. The only blemish is a handful of leftover temporary test-listener log/pid files in /tmp, a low-severity, non-security-impacting residue.\",\"limitations\":[\"The self-curl test intended to prove an unrelated port (9999) is blocked was inconclusive because same-host curl traverses the loopback interface, which bypasses the public-zone chain; unrelated-port rejection instead relies on nftables ruleset inspection rather than a live external-connection test.\",\"No evidence was captured from a genuinely external client verifying SSH/8080 reachability or unrelated-port rejection from outside the node itself; all functional tests were run locally on node1.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Enable a persistent host firewall on node1 (firewalld active, enabled, and permanent config in place)","status":"satisfied","summary":"firewalld was already active/enabled at baseline; executor added persistent (--permanent) rules for ssh and 8080/tcp, set zone target to REJECT, and reloaded. /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml on disk shows the persisted config, and post-reboot the same config was confirmed intact with firewalld active/enabled.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d107a6a41b744c99","cmd-a6b52ea9171c46ac","cmd-953425bdcd824c85"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Permit SSH inbound","status":"satisfied","summary":"firewall-cmd --list-all shows ssh service allowed both at runtime and permanent; nftables filter_IN_public_allow chain accepts tcp dport 22; sshd confirmed listening and healthy pre- and post-restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d107a6a41b744c99","cmd-7ef75988122f4e4d","cmd-953425bdcd824c85"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Permit TCP port 8080 inbound","status":"satisfied","summary":"firewall-cmd shows 8080/tcp added and persisted; nftables allow chain accepts tcp dport 8080; live curl test to the node's external IP on 8080 returned HTTP 200 confirming functional reachability through the zone rules.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d107a6a41b744c99","cmd-7ef75988122f4e4d","cmd-c36bc3202faa49f4"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Reject unrelated inbound connections","status":"satisfied","summary":"Zone target set to %%REJECT%%; nftables filter_IN_public chain falls through to 'reject with icmpx admin-prohibited' for traffic not matching the allow chain (only 22/8080). Pre-existing unrelated allowances (cockpit, dhcpv6-client) were removed so only ssh+8080 remain. The self-curl test on port 9999 returned content rather than a clean rejection, but this is explained and consistent with loopback (iifname lo accept) bypassing the public-zone chain rather than a real misconfiguration — the nftables ruleset directly shows the reject fallback applies to the eth0-bound public zone.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b39b793c55464edc","cmd-deed77eb98f64c31","cmd-c36bc3202faa49f4"]},{"id":"req-5","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id (4a743885...) and firewalld health captured; systemctl reboot issued and acknowledged; subsequent poll timed out confirming disconnect; post-restart boot_id (2a24f144...) differs, confirmed by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots as well; firewalld, persisted zone config, nftables rules, and sshd were all re-verified healthy after the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e44e795edde44b5","cmd-09c8fa3c79e1459e","cmd-2934e7b357fa4d93","cmd-7c1d8292f3044eac","cmd-953425bdcd824c85","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"State-changing commands were limited to the firewalld reconfiguration (required), removal of unrelated pre-existing service allowances (required to satisfy the 'reject unrelated' outcome), temporary test HTTP listeners on 8080/9999 used for bounded functional verification, and the restart itself. The test listeners were killed and confirmed absent from the socket table (cmd-f766d31253d84359, cmd-a6b52ea9171c46ac), but their log/pid files (/tmp/http8080.log, /tmp/http8080.pid, /tmp/http9999.log, /tmp/http9999.pid) remained in the after-executor temporary-files snapshot as minor uncleaned residue — low-risk and non-functional but not fully reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b39b793c55464edc","cmd-c36bc3202faa49f4","cmd-f766d31253d84359","cmd-a6b52ea9171c46ac","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task — a persistent firewalld configuration on node1 permitting only SSH and 8080/tcp while rejecting other inbound traffic — are directly supported by firewall-cmd, nftables, and live-port evidence, and the configuration was confirmed to survive an actual node restart (differing boot_id, recovered firewalld/nftables/sshd state). The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also completed with clear pre/post boot-identity and health evidence. The only blemish is a handful of leftover temporary test-listener log/pid files in /tmp, a low-severity, non-security-impacting residue.","limitations":["The self-curl test intended to prove an unrelated port (9999) is blocked was inconclusive because same-host curl traverses the loopback interface, which bypasses the public-zone chain; unrelated-port rejection instead relies on nftables ruleset inspection rather than a live external-connection test.","No evidence was captured from a genuinely external client verifying SSH/8080 reachability or unrelated-port rejection from outside the node itself; all functional tests were run locally on node1."]},"ttft_ms":17221,"type":"result","duration_ms":51299,"uuid":"33d9fe7d-8595-46c0-8fee-f806a8f1ed8f","ttft_stream_ms":1286,"time_to_request_ms":192,"first_content_frame_ms":1286,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
